<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chandrabhanu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Chandrabhanu Sridhamaraja</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chandrabhanu Sridhamaraja was a king of Tambralinga on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a> in the 13th century, known from an inscription at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaiya">Chaiya</a> dated 1230. He built up a navy and invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> twice, in 1247 and again around 1260, seeking among other things its Buddhist relics, and for a time held part of the north. He was defeated by Pandyan forces in the 1260s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chandrabhanu.jpg" alt="Chandrabhanu" width="320" height="495" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahoerstemeier · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nakhon_Si_Thammarat_Chedi_Phra_Baromathat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
